WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.696
The beautiful ballerina gracefully stepped back from the front of the stage.

2
00:00:05.697 --> 00:00:12.574
She took one last bow as the curtain closed again and hid her from the audience.

3
00:00:12.575 --> 00:00:21.407
Immediately, the children were surrounded by a swarm of people—dancers, costumers, and stagehands.

4
00:00:21.408 --> 00:00:25.629
Everyone ignored Vinnie and Mandy.

5
00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:31.690
"Anna! Bravo! You were magical!" cried a nearby gentleman.

6
00:00:31.691 --> 00:00:36.491
He smiled at the ballerina as she walked toward him.

7
00:00:36.492 --> 00:00:39.617
She held an armful of roses.

8
00:00:39.618 --> 00:00:43.653
More flowers lay scattered on the stage.

9
00:00:43.654 --> 00:00:46.417
"Bring them to my dressing room,"

10
00:00:46.418 --> 00:00:51.482
ordered the ballerina, throwing the bundle of roses to Mandy.

11
00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:55.072
"But I . . . ," Mandy began.

12
00:00:55.073 --> 00:00:58.459
The dancer brushed past her.

13
00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.592
A man shouted at Vinnie:

14
00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:04.888
"You! Collect all of Miss Pavlova’s flowers!"

15
00:01:04.889 --> 00:01:09.754
He shoved Vinnie out onto the stage.

16
00:01:09.755 --> 00:01:13.540
Someone pushed Mandy toward the dancer.

17
00:01:13.541 --> 00:01:17.188
"Hurry up!" the ballerina ordered.

18
00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:19.918
Mandy followed her.

19
00:01:19.919 --> 00:01:23.460
She couldn’t see where Vinnie had gone.

20
00:01:23.461 --> 00:01:29.113
In the ballerina’s dressing room, Mandy stood nervously by the door.

21
00:01:29.114 --> 00:01:32.355
Anna and the gentleman were arguing.

22
00:01:32.356 --> 00:01:34.981
"You are my manager, Victor!

23
00:01:34.982 --> 00:01:38.945
I wanted to dance in my other ballet shoes!"

24
00:01:38.946 --> 00:01:42.396
she cried, stamping her feet.

25
00:01:42.397 --> 00:01:43.868
"I’m sorry, Anna.

26
00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:49.977
Next time, I will bring all your shoes," Victor apologized.

27
00:01:49.978 --> 00:01:54.078
They talked loudly and with so much passion.

28
00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:57.273
Mandy watched them fascinated.

29
00:01:57.274 --> 00:02:01.814
"Where had Vinnie and I landed?" she wondered.

30
00:02:01.815 --> 00:02:04.776
"Girl! What are you staring at?"

31
00:02:04.777 --> 00:02:07.570
Anna was speaking to her.

32
00:02:07.571 --> 00:02:13.026
"Oh, I’m sorry, ma’am," she apologized.

33
00:02:13.027 --> 00:02:17.542
"Your flowers . . ." Mandy held them out.

34
00:02:17.543 --> 00:02:20.501
"Take them to my carriage and wait.

35
00:02:20.502 --> 00:02:23.006
You’re the new girl, right?

36
00:02:23.007 --> 00:02:26.755
Sergei said Tatiana was sick tonight."

37
00:02:26.756 --> 00:02:32.620
Then Anna waved her arm in a way that told Mandy to leave.

38
00:02:32.621 --> 00:02:38.738
After collecting the flowers from the stage, Vinnie was given a broom.

39
00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:42.167
"Are you new here?" asked a young boy.

40
00:02:42.168 --> 00:02:46.625
He was about Vinnie’s age and was already sweeping.

41
00:02:46.626 --> 00:02:52.878
"I guess," replied Vinnie, wondering where "here" was.

42
00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:57.745
"I’m Mikhail. What’s your name?" asked the boy.

43
00:02:57.746 --> 00:03:00.472
Vinnie introduced himself.

44
00:03:00.473 --> 00:03:06.463
Both he and the boy were dressed in dark trousers and shirts.

45
00:03:06.464 --> 00:03:09.514
"She’s a beautiful dancer,"

46
00:03:09.515 --> 00:03:13.134
said Vinnie, starting up a conversation.

47
00:03:13.135 --> 00:03:17.280
He hoped Mikhail would reveal where they were.

48
00:03:17.281 --> 00:03:23.947
"Anna Pavlova is Russia’s most famous ballerina," Mikhail said proudly.

49
00:03:23.948 --> 00:03:28.868
"She just came back from a tour of Europe and the United States."

50
00:03:28.869 --> 00:03:33.138
"Russia!" Vinnie said to himself.

51
00:03:33.139 --> 00:03:39.448
Meanwhile, Mandy was riding away in a carriage with Anna and Victor.

52
00:03:39.449 --> 00:03:44.200
As she looked back, Mandy gasped at the grand building.

53
00:03:44.201 --> 00:03:50.153
"What a gorgeous theater!" cried Mandy.

54
00:03:50.154 --> 00:03:55.855
"The Mariinsky Theater has brought me much success," Anna said softly.

55
00:03:55.856 --> 00:03:58.613
She seemed happier now.

56
00:03:58.614 --> 00:04:01.813
She blew the theater a kiss.

57
00:04:01.814 --> 00:04:11.139
"For your next tour," began Victor, "we will travel on the Trans-Siberian Railway to Vladivostok, and then we’ll go . . ."

58
00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:14.134
Anna grew angry again.

59
00:04:14.135 --> 00:04:19.090
"What? I just got back! I need to rest!"

60
00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:23.071
"But, Anna," Victor said calmly.

61
00:04:23.072 --> 00:04:27.836
"Your fans all across the motherland want to see you dance!"

62
00:04:27.837 --> 00:04:31.838
Mandy looked out the window, amazed.

63
00:04:31.839 --> 00:04:37.631
"Vladivostok? We’re in Russia!" she thought.

64
00:04:37.632 --> 00:04:41.947
Anna cried, "I will stay in St. Petersburg.

65
00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.994
I am tired, Victor!

66
00:04:43.995 --> 00:04:49.776
I will not discuss this anymore!"

